  "jobTitle": "Software Developer",
  "summary": "I’m a Technical Lead and Senior Software Developer with over 20 years of experience designing, developing, modernizing, and supporting enterprise software solutions across financial services, government, healthcare, cybersecurity, telecommunications, insurance, and retail.\n \nThroughout my career, I’ve worked across the full software development lifecycle—from solution and database design to front-end development, APIs, integrations, cloud services, production support, and technical leadership.\n \nMy core technology experience includes C#/.NET, Angular, TypeScript, JavaScript, SQL Server, PostgreSQL, Python/FastAPI, REST APIs, Entity Framework, Dapper, Azure, and AWS.\n \nAt BBD, I’ve contributed to and led solutions for organizations including SARS, Absa, Standard Bank, SA Taxi/Mobalize, GOMO, SecHQ, and GetCare. My experience ranges from modern Angular applications and Python microservices to financial platforms, workflow systems, mobile solutions, data-processing applications, and complex enterprise integrations.\n \nIn my current Technical Lead role, I’m working on SARS risk systems, where I’ve redesigned database structures, re-engineered XML processing and data normalization components, and developed calculation and rules-engine functionality to improve the accuracy, maintainability, and flexibility of risk assessment solutions.\n \nPreviously, on SecHQ, I worked with Angular 15/19 and Python FastAPI microservices, developing responsive user interfaces, REST APIs, RBAC functionality, and reusable Angular components while mentoring developers and providing technical guidance and code reviews.\n \nOne of my strengths is the ability to adapt to new technologies and complex business domains. My career has taken me from VB6, WinForms, Silverlight and WPF through to modern Angular, .NET APIs, Python microservices, PostgreSQL, serverless Azure solutions, AWS, and AI-assisted development.\n \nAs a Technical Lead, I remain hands-on with development while mentoring developers, solving complex technical problems, improving architecture and engineering practices, and helping teams translate business requirements into scalable, maintainable software.\n \nI’m passionate about technology, continuous learning, technical leadership, and building software that delivers meaningful business value.",
